@startuml
!include style.iuml
title Customer journey 5: rent a GPU VM, connect, compute and release
actor Customer as C
boundary "Public API\nNGINX" as E
participant "Gateway / Hydra\nprovisioning control" as H
participant "Provider API\nor Atlas adapter" as P
participant "GPU VM guest\nSSH / lyceum user" as V
database "Volumes / snapshots\nprovider storage" as D
participant "CPU / GPU\nRAM / VRAM" as G
actor "Employee / automation\nadmin identity" as A
actor "Provider operator\nBMC / hypervisor / physical" as O

C -[#16803C]> E : [ENC] HTTPS: authenticated request, region/SKU, SSH public key
E -[#DC2626]> H : [PLAIN] Gateway HTTP backend\nAuthorize account / resource ownership
alt External provider API
H -[#D4A000]> P : [CHECK] Provider-specific API authentication and transport\nCapture effective endpoint, scopes and site admission
else Atlas control path
H -[#DC2626]> P : [PLAIN] Configured http://atlas with bearer token\nIndependent mesh coverage must be demonstrated
end
P -[#D4A000]> V : [CHECK] Provider creates guest / boot image / devices\nBoot trust, firmware and hypervisor evidence missing
H -[#D4A000]> V : [CHECK] SSH bootstrap is encrypted but host key unchecked (F11)
V -[#DC2626]> D : [PLAIN] Guest formats/mounts filesystem without LUKS\nProvider encryption below guest remains UNKNOWN
H -[#D4A000]> V : [CHECK] SSH handover: remove root/ubuntu authorized keys\nNot proof of removal of every administrative identity (F24)
H -[#DC2626]> E : [PLAIN] Gateway HTTP response: VM connection details
E -[#16803C]> C : [ENC] HTTPS: address / connection information
C -[#D4A000]> V : [CHECK] SSH encrypted; customer host-fingerprint\nverification not established by this repository
V -[#DC2626]> V : [PLAIN] Customer commands / secrets in process memory
V -[#D4A000]> G : [CHECK] Compute: CPU/GPU link and memory protection\nNo attestation-based admission / key release established
G -[#D4A000]> V : [CHECK] Results in workload-visible memory
V -[#D4A000]> D : [CHECK] Data persistence / optional snapshots\nProvider encryption, key custody and copies need evidence
V -[#D4A000]> C : [CHECK] SSH result stream; host identity caveat remains
group Administrative exposure (capability, not a normal customer request)
A -[#D4A000]> H : [CHECK] IAM / SOPS / CI / provisioning authority\nBroad grants and shared secret access (F05/F12)
A -[#D4A000]> V : [CHECK] Any retained guest/support access must be enumerated\nHandover is not a complete revocation proof
O -[#D4A000]> V : [CHECK] Potential console / host / hypervisor access\nAuthorization and physical controls not evidenced per site
O -[#D4A000]> D : [CHECK] Potential media/snapshot access\nEncryption and operator separation require provider evidence
O -[#D4A000]> G : [CHECK] Potential debug / physical / host access\nConfidential GPU boundary not established
end
C -[#16803C]> E : [ENC] HTTPS: release VM / request data deletion
E -[#DC2626]> H : [PLAIN] Gateway HTTP delete request
H -[#D4A000]> P : [CHECK] Provider-specific deletion / volume lifecycle\nNo end-to-end attested erasure guarantee established
note over V,O
Apply separately to each actual provider/datacenter in section 5.
Guest plaintext is not proof that provider physical media is unencrypted.
No administrative-access arrow claims an employee actually read data.
end note
@enduml
